{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1793349566,"nonce":"CHLEWEwUceh+1nx+44ZotmbeESA=","target":"d1a05d63d5db5e97ea126c14c36ed038193ad9fe03b1b5a95ea33b85d27f3006","message":"Committed locally as f333e61f2e2923df9d5b97d93618d7dad95338e3.\n\nSupported native Div background isolation owners now retain glass, native paint and collected content at their background anchor. Compatible ancestors join that ordered graph, including painted descendants beneath motion wrappers. Transparent wrappers propagate a child's background anchor. Inert ordinary roots without a background glass scope retain the existing first-level foreground glass path. CSS opacity owners are resolved through the existing stable-to-layout mapping and retained at settled endpoints.\n\nThe original 300a50f5 runtime negative at (60,60) was [64,128,64,255], expected [0,128,128,255]. /private/tmp/blinc-glass-background-negative.log. The final joint-opacity control passes all four app frame modes and also checks the glass material outside the image, which samples unattenuated parent paint before joint opacity.\n\nOwned background bakes snapshot prior paint for each glass command. Before entering an isolated child with glass, the parent's prefix is retained as its inherited backdrop. Straightening the local premultiplied target preserves translucent ancestor paint. Snapshot sampling never reads the current render attachment, and later paint is excluded. GPU callback/mesh output is already present in that prefix; it is not replayed to construct the sample. Background/backdrop dispatch shares one bake. Explicit prepared-backdrop foreground dispatch is unchanged.\n\nTen new offscreen controls cover joint opacity; mixed native/plain/styled text, SVG, image and canvas content; unified/legacy and samples1/4; DPI1/2; all four app frame modes and repeated/cached replay; moving wrappers, background/foreground sibling order and opacity endpoints;