t straight-alpha copy of the current layer. Inherited snapshots remain live while their child renders, so active isolation depth increases memory. Additional panels increase snapshot work and bandwidth. For RGBA8 each frame snapshot alone costs roughly4*frame_width*frame_height bytes, in addition to existing owner/effect layers and tight glass surfaces. Released textures follow the existing pool policy. Foreground glass keeps its prior direct/tight path. No frame-time or peak-memory benchmark, and no mobile/browser performance claim.\n\nAPI: additive PrimitiveBatch::has_background_glass query; internal recorder/renderer metadata changes. No shader, primitive/instance/uniform layout, shared ABI/ClipPath record or stable-ID change. Prior glass API and GlassUniforms32 release review remains required.\n\nParent e0a7502 remains open for nested/unsupported glass/portal/flow/3D mixtures, arbitrary prior external destination samples, independent-pass/persistent named sampling and separate low-level contexts. Owned-background prior-paint sampling is covered here, not arbitrary existing TextureView-only destination pixels. Version/API, actual Cargo package, hosted and device/browser verification remain. Main twenty commits ahead of recorded origin/main. No push/publication or desktop input.","files":null}]}